    {
      "text": "within ye are full of hypocrisy and iniquity, Matt. 23:28. because iniquity shall abound, the love of many shall wax cold, Matt. 24:12 (D&C 45:27; JS—M 1:10, 30). purchased a field with the reward of iniquity, Acts 1:18. turning away every one of you from his iniquities, Acts 3:26. Rejoiceth not in iniquity, but rejoiceth in the truth, 1 Cor. 13:6. mystery of iniquity doth already work, 2 Thes. 2:7. nameth the name of Christ depart from iniquity, 2 Tim. 2:19. redeem us from all iniquity, Titus 2:14. hast loved righteousness, and hated iniquity, Heb. 1:9. their iniquities will I remember no more, Heb. 8:12 (10:17). tongue is a fire, a world of iniquity, James 3:6.",
